comments.body:
@randomstuff - for me, 2.11.1 is an in-depth defense, an extra step further from the basic security level. If you integrate an application with an untrusted IdP, you'll have problems anyway.

1.2.6 as a pre-condition security decision requirement for 2.2.1, which is an L1 requirement. So most likely, we need to align those and put 1.2.6 to L1 as well.

For background information - first we had many of password-related requirements a level 2, but... as in practice password-related requirements are mostly relevant only for L1 (from L2 we require MFA), then we changed many of them (back) to L1.
